.TH WEIGHTRAIL 1 "2026-07-11" "Weightrail 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weightrail \- record and review local weight measurements
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weightrail
.RI [ options ] " [weight|stats]"
.br
.B weight-tracker
.RI [ options ] " [weight|stats]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Weightrail is a local-first terminal weight tracker.  It stores measurements
in a per-user SQLite database and never requires a service or network account.
The command
.B weight-tracker
is a compatibility name for
.BR weightrail .
.SH COMMANDS AND OPTIONS
A positional
.I weight
records or updates today's date in the Asia/Taipei timezone.
The positional command
.B stats
prints basic statistics.
.TP
.B --show
Show recorded rows, a terminal graph when the optional plotext dependency is
available, and a trend summary.
.TP
.B --stats
Show basic statistics.
.TP
.B --summary
Show the numeric trend summary.
.TP
.BI --import " FILE"
Import CSV data with the header date,weight_kg.
.TP
.BI --db-path " PATH"
Use a specific SQLite database path.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B HOME
determines the default data location.  Use
.B --db-path
to keep data in another location, including one selected through local XDG
configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/weight-tracker-cli/weights.sqlite
Default per-user SQLite database.  Package removal and purge do not delete it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for application errors.  Argument parsing errors use the
standard argparse nonzero status.
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/SleepyMario/weight-tracker-cli
